<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18586" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">formīdābĭlĭs</span></b> ,
			e, adj.
		1. formido, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>causing fear</i>, <i>terrible</i>,
				<i>formidable</i> (<b>poet.</b>
			and in post-class. prose; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">formidolosus): lumen,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					2, 857</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nec formidabilis ulli,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 2, 174</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Orcus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 14, 116</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aspectus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell.
					14, 4, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sonus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					19, 1, 17</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dolores et metus, per se formidabiles res,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Ep. 123, 14</span></i>
			.—In the <i>neutr.</i> adverbially: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">formidabile ridens,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 8, 582</span></i>
			.</div>
